A Rust tuple bundles several values of different types into one value. Tuples have a fixed length: once declared, they cannot grow or shrink in size.[1] You can give the type explicitly, as in this example:

```rust
fn main() {
    let tup: (i32, f64, u8) = (500, 6.4, 1);
}
